  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale  \n**Objective**: Minimize the maximum overlap integral C by finding a step function h that avoids significant overlap with its translations. The solution leverages a combination of:  \n- **Regularized Fourier coefficients** to generate structured initial candidates  \n- **Projected gradient descent** adapted for the discrete form arial of optimization  \n- **Adaptive penalty scaling** to enforce both the integral constraint and boundary conditions  \nThe approach improves upon the previous local search by emphasizing global exploration through gradient-based optimization and introducing covariance adaptation for promising regions.  \n\n2. Mathematical specification  \n**Variables**: h \u2208 [0, 1]<sup>n</sup> with \u2211h = n/2.  \n**Objective**: Minimize C = (2/n)\u00d7<sup>max<sub>k</sub></sup>\u27e8h, (1\u2212h)<sub>k</sub\u27e9\u27e9  \n**Constraints**:  \n- 0 \u2264 h<sup>(i)</sup> \u2264 1 \u2200i  \n- \u2211<sup>i</sup>h<sup>(i)</sup> = n/2  \n**Representation**: h = 0.5 + 0.5<sup>a</sup> where a \u2208 \u211d<sup>n</sup> corresponds to discrete sine components at normalized frequencies.  \n**Formulation**: Minimize max<sub>k</sub> \u27e8h, (1-h)_k\u27e9 using projected gradient with:  \n\u2207_h [ \u27e8h, (1-h)_k\u27e9 ] = (1-h) + h<sup>T</sup>diag(-h)_k  \nProjected step: P<sub>[0,1]</sub>(x) = Clip(x, 0, 1)  \n\n3. Implementation procedure  \n**Initialization**:  \n- Use initial_h_values if provided; else generate via PhaseAmplitudeScaling(shape=1000) with frequency resolution 1/np.sqrt(n)  \n- Normalize to satisfy \u2211h = n/2 via scaling  \n**Main loop**:  \n- Empirically select penalty weight \u03c4 = max(\u03bc\u2098\u2099 \u00d7 ln(t_remain), 1e-6)  \n- Solve using coordinate descent with projection:  \n  h\u209c+1 = Clip(h\u209c - \u03b1\u27e8\u2207h, (1-h)_k\u27e9\u27e9\u03bc\u209c, 0, 1)  \n**Adaptation**:  \n- Track covariance via exponential moving average (span=100) from solution trajectory  \n- Restart from sampled covariance points when gradient dominance exceeds 0.99  \n- Maintain history of improving overlap references for pareto ranking  \n\n4. Search choices  \n**Starting points**: Covariance-adapted points from past optima with optional Poisson jitter  \n**Local vs. global**: Balance by adjusting \u03bc\u2098\u2099 linearly between [25, 100] depending on \u2207 curvature  \n**Fallback**: Downsample whenever projection exceeds 3 invalid points; use nearest neighbor interpolation when resolution drops below 50%  \n\n5. Compute budget  \n- Est. n_moperations: O(n\u00d7budget_s) but accelerated by diagonalization  \n- Check \u03c4\u2714 when time_remaining > 5 seconds and overlap < current_best + 0.1  \n- Parallelize gradient checks across core frequencies (up to min(4, n/core_size))  \n- CPU-bound; 1-core scaling: budget_s/60 minutes = n  \n\n6. Validation and contract  \n- Return (h, check_overlap(h), n_grain) manually  \n- Ensure \u2211h = n/2 with supply\u03b4=1e-3 and bounds met by projection  \n- Re-evaluate C5 via reduce_overlap(h, grain=5) for verification  \n- Maintain history of top 3 C5 records across resolution trials",
